01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Devil's Advocate is a 1997 American supernatural horror film directed by Taylor Hackford, written by
Jonathan Lemkin and Tony Gilroy, and starring Keanu Reeves, Al Pacino and Charlize Theron.

12
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Based on Andrew Neiderman's 1990 novel, it is about a gifted young Florida
lawyer invited to work for a major New York City law firm.

13
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
As his wife becomes haunted by frightening visions, the lawyer slowly
realizes that the firm's owner, John Milton, is the Devil.

14
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The name John Milton is one of several allusions to Paradise Lost, as well
as to Dante Alighieri's Inferno and the legend of Faust.

15
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
An adaptation of Neiderman's novel went into a development hell during the
1990s, with Hackford gaining control of the production.

16
01:36:00,000 --> 01:36:06,000
Filming took place around New York City and Florida.

17
01:42:00,000 --> 01:42:06,000
Devil's Advocate received mixed reviews, with critics crediting it
for entertainment value and Pacino's performance.

